    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d343">

                <pb facs="0739" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg729"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 941.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 7, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch, No. 658, relative to the
                    alleged violation of the British foreign enlistment act by Captain Winslow, of
                    the Kearsarge, having been submitted to the Secretary of the Navy, this
                    department is informed by him, in a letter of yesterday, that it would not
                    comport with the interests of the service to order that vessel home at present,
                    with a view to a further formal investigation of the charge, which the British
                    government seems to expect. Upon her first return to the United States, however,
                    the inquiry referred to will be directed, should such then be the wish of her
                    Britannic Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
